# Native Apple license scope

This additional MIT grant covers the independently implemented native Apple
application source and generated artwork in the following release input roots:

- apple/App, except the third-party ReaderAssets distributions and license notices
- apple/Presentation, apple/Playback, apple/Adoption
- apple/Export/Sources/YearExport
- apple/Localization/Sources/NativeLocalization and apple/Localization/translations
- apple/Diagnostics/Sources/NativeDiagnostics
- apple/Migration/Sources/LegacyMigration
- tvos/App and tvos/Core/Sources/TVCore

It also covers the fork-created Apple build configuration, scripts and localization
generator. Historical inherited translation inputs are no longer used or bundled.
Third-party reader libraries retain their respective licenses (EPUB.js BSD-2-Clause,
JSZip MIT, and the accompanying embedded dependency notices). Apple SDKs and
frameworks remain subject to Apple's licenses.

This grant does not cover the repository's inherited code, Android code, legacy
Realm exporter/models or compatibility fixtures, upstream translations, historical
patches, or other third-party materials. Their existing licenses remain unchanged.
The repository-root GPL license is retained. Interoperability identifiers and the
independent project's origin disclosure are preserved.

